.TH LS 1 "October 2026" "OS Assignment 02" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ls \- list directory contents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./bin/ls
.RB [ \-l ]
.RB [ \-x ]
.RB [ \-R ]
.RI [ directory ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B ls
program lists the contents of directories. It supports basic listing, long-format output, horizontal listing, alphabetical sorting, colorized output, and recursive directory listing.
.PP
If no directory is specified, the program lists the contents of the current directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-l
Display files in long format, including file permissions, number of links, owner, group, file size, modification time, and filename.
.TP
.B \-x
Display filenames horizontally, filling each row before moving to the next row.
.TP
.B \-R
List directories recursively, including the contents of their subdirectories.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Alphabetical sorting
Filenames are sorted alphabetically.
.TP
.B Colorized output
Files and directories are displayed in colors according to their types, where supported by the terminal.
.TP
.B Directory handling
The program reads directory entries and retrieves file metadata.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ./bin/ls
List the current directory.
.TP
.B ./bin/ls -l
Display a detailed listing.
.TP
.B ./bin/ls -x
Display filenames horizontally.
.TP
.B ./bin/ls -R
List directories recursively.
.TP
.B ./bin/ls -lR
Display detailed listings recursively.
.SH IMPLEMENTATION
This program is implemented in C and uses directory operations, file metadata functions, dynamic memory allocation, command-line option parsing, sorting, terminal-width detection, ANSI color codes, and recursion.
.SH LIMITATIONS
This is a simplified implementation of the Unix
.B ls
command and does not support every option available in the standard system utility.
.SH AUTHOR
Faria Azhar
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ls (1),
.BR stat (2),
.BR opendir (3),
.BR readdir (3)
